I have completed the deep adversarial review of the DaoStream v2 staged changes. The findings have been synthesized into an Implementation Plan artifact. 

The review surfaced 4 critical P1 defects related to concurrency (an `append!` race condition), idempotency (`close!` breaking the attachment freeze), portability (invalid UUIDs in descriptors), and testing invariants (the oracle hardcoding mock cursor internals). 

Please review the [dao_stream_review_plan.md](conversation://1d9719fb-c044-4e55-a0ad-07771d2a2fa2) artifact. If you approve the findings and proposed fixes, you can proceed by clicking "Proceed" on the artifact, and I will apply the fixes to the staged files.
